 I'd be happy to help you create a JavaScript function that accepts text and posts it to a specified Slack channel using the Slack API. Here's an example of how you might implement this:

```javascript
const axios = require('axios'); // Make sure to install 'axios' package before running the code

async function postMessageToSlackChannel(text, channel) {
  try {
    const url = 'https://slack.com/api/chat.postMessage';
    const token = process.env.SLACK_BOT_TOKEN; // Replace with your bot token

    const data = {
      channel: channel,
      text: text,
    };

    const response = await axios.post(url, data, {
      headers: {
        'Content-Type': 'application/json',
        Authorization: `Bearer ${token}`,
      },
    });

    if (response.data.ok) {
      console.log(`Message posted successfully to channel #${channel}: ${text}`);
    } else {
      throw new Error(`Error posting message: ${response.data.error}`);
    }
  } catch (err) {
    console.error(`Error posting message to Slack: ${err.message}`);
  }
}

// Usage example
postMessageToSlackChannel('Hello, world!', '#general');
```

This example uses the `axios` library to make HTTP requests to the Slack API. Make sure to install the `axios` package by running `npm install axios`. Also, replace the `SLACK_BOT_TOKEN` variable with your actual bot token. The function accepts the text and channel name as arguments and sends them as a JSON payload to the Slack API. The function logs a success message upon successful execution, or an error message if something goes wrong.

