 I'd be happy to help you write a PowerShell script to recursively check folders for Access Control Lists (ACLs) that reference Security Identifiers (SIDs) which only appear in the SID history of any user or group in the Active Directory domain. Here's an outline of how you can accomplish this:

1. First, we need to retrieve all the SIDs from the Active Directory using the `Get-ADObject` cmdlet. We will store these SIDs in a hash table with the key being the SID and the value being the name of the object (user or group).

```powershell
# Function to get all SIDs and their corresponding names from AD
function Get-ADSids {
    $ADSids = @{}
    $Filter = 'objectClass -eq "user" -or objectClass -eq "group"'
    $Searcher = New-Object -ComObject "ADSIisearcher"
    $Searcher.Filter = $Filter
    $Searcher.PropertiesToLoad = 'sAMAccountName, DistinguishedName'
    do {
        $Results = $Searcher.FindAll() | Where-Object {$_.Properties.Count -ge 2}
        foreach ($Result in $Results) {
            $ADSids[$Result.Properties['sID']] = $Result.Properties['DistinguishedName'].Split('\')[-1]
        }
    } while ($Searcher.HasMoreResults)
    return $ADSids
}
```

